Implement GetLocalAddresses() on POSIX (getifaddrs), replacing the
upstream stub that returns false everywhere except Windows.

Without it, GNS's own ICE client cannot work at all on Linux/macOS:
CSteamNetworkingICESession::GatherInterfaces() (steamnetworkingsockets_stun.cpp)
bails the moment GetLocalAddresses() returns false, so the interface list
stays empty, no host candidates are ever produced, no candidate messages
are ever sent, and the ICE transport neither connects nor fails -- it just
sits there. Observed exactly that here: both peers logged
"CConnectionTransportP2PICE_Valve::Init" and queued an "Initial ICE auth"
rendezvous, then nothing further, and every connection fell back to the
gateway-relayed DataChannel transport.

Mirrors the Windows implementation deliberately: same AF_INET/AF_INET6
handling, same "skip loopback via IsLocalHost()" rule, same convention
that the return value means "the enumeration ran" (an empty list is a
valid result). Interfaces that are down are skipped, which
GetAdaptersAddresses effectively does on Windows. Link-local 169.254.x.x
is deliberately NOT filtered here -- GatherInterfaces() already drops it.

Android below API 24 keeps the upstream stub: bionic only declares
getifaddrs()/freeifaddrs() from API 24 onwards, and this project still
builds an API 19 target.

